h96-kernel-switch (8.0.0~r16) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initramfs hook copies one hex dumper only (gnuod, else hexdump; any
    file over 1 MiB skipped): r15 copied Rust coreutils multicall binary
    once per tool name (51 MB unpacked, uInitrd +23 MB). Scratch
    mkinitramfs: +56 KB compressed, +79 KB unpacked over no hook.
    init-bottom script uses busybox applets for sed, grep, cut, tr,
    basename, uname and mount.
  * staged.meta records offsets of build-id notes instead of size, mtime
    and inode; init-bottom reads build ids of staged Image there, so
    copy of rootfs into image (new inodes) keeps initramfs mount working
    and changed staged Image leaves decision to boot unit.

 -- Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000

h96-kernel-switch (8.0.0~r15) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initramfs init-bottom script and hook: before switch_root, running
    build differs from staged Image (build ids in staged.meta, trusted
    while size, mtime and inode of staged Image match), saved tree of
    running build mounted read-only on real root, so modules PID1 loads
    at startup (ipv6) and first modprobe@ units already match (box: 3
    BTF validation failures per fallback boot on r14). Every uInitrd
    that try builds carries it; modules unit stays second line.
  * modprobe@.service drop-in: After=h96-kernel-switch-modules.service.
  * list marks generation running by GNU build id of its Image; banner
    only when build id is missing (identical banners marked both).
  * snapshot-modules prints mounted-tree upgrade notice without --quiet
    too. Manual: generation numbers reused after prune.

 -- Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0000

h96-kernel-switch (8.0.0~r14) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Module tree per kernel build: two builds of one release share
    /usr/lib/modules/KREL and package upgrade replaces it, so fallback to
    earlier build loaded modules of newer build (BTF Invalid argument: no
    WiFi, GPU, compositor). Tool saves tree of each staged build under
    /var/lib/h96-kernel-switch/modules (hard links, keyed by Image sha256
    and GNU build id): at try, from apt hook before dpkg
    (/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/80h96-kernel-switch) and from postinst.
  * New h96-kernel-switch-modules.service, before systemd-udevd and
    systemd-modules-load: running build differs from package tree, saved
    tree of running build mounted read-only over /usr/lib/modules/KREL.
    Enabled with first saved tree.
  * try of other build of in-boot release refused unless module tree of
    in-boot build is saved or found in h96-kernel deb (apt cache, offline
    repo). Initramfs built from package tree also while saved tree mounted.
  * New commands snapshot-modules, repair-modules, modules-mount; status
    prints module tree source per generation and WARN line when running
    build has no matching tree (list prints WARN too); confirm, prune and
    try drop saved trees no staged or /boot Image needs.

 -- Scrumpper <190908034+Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

h96-kernel-switch (8.0.0~r13) resolute; urgency=medium

  * try of release that is already default or running (or that current
    Image embeds) makes new generation when staged Image or DTB differs
    from in-boot generation; refused as before when both are equal.
  * Boot guard and confirm tell trial boot from fallback by Image banner
    (build number and date) when generations of same release differ
    there, else by boot id and h96ks/cur as before.
  * list prints generations under each release with roles default,
    trial, trial-previous, rollback-target and running; status prints
    generation lines; in-use and prune take generation names KREL.gN.

